    "narrative": "For today\u2019s slate, **Daulton Varsho** (67.02) and **Lawrence Butler** (63.32) headline our offensive output. **Daulton Varsho** benefits significantly from a favorable matchup against Burrows, where a combination of a hitter-friendly park and a +10% boost from a platoon advantage propels him into the upper echelon of our daily rankings. Similarly, **Lawrence Butler** is poised for a strong performance against Mahle; his elite platoon edge (+13%) and strong SP skill rating solidify his status as a must-start. **Geraldo Perdomo** (63.13) and **Tyler Freeman** (61.08) also provide substantial value, both earning high efficiency scores largely due to their premium spots in the batting order, which remains the primary catalyst for our run-scoring potential.\n\nThe most difficult roster decision today involved the marginal slot occupied by **Jung Hoo Lee** (42.81). While he makes the lineup, he sits precariously close to our \"below floor\" threshold. His score was dragged down by a combination of the opposing catcher\u2019s elite pop time and a disadvantageous platoon split against the lefty, Jump. The optimizer considered benching him for a safer defensive outlook, but his baseline projection remains just high enough to retain his spot. We continue to monitor the status of our injured core, specifically **Jos\u00e9 Ram\u00edrez**, **Will Smith**, **Dylan Beavers**, and **Ryan Waldschmidt**; their continued absence on the IL remains a significant drag on our ceiling, leaving players like **Jeremiah Jackson** and **Jonathan Aranda** to shoulder heavier loads despite lower individual efficiency scores. Be advised that while **Bryson Stott** (60.03) projects well, his matchup against Palmquist features a catcher with a 1.89s pop time, which slightly caps his upside in the stolen base department despite the favorable SP delivery metrics.",
